                             PCBoard v15.4 HISTORY
                             =====================

04/22/97  17:16   PCBOARD.EXE
=============================
- Fixed the 'L' command.  Wasn't locating any filespec by using wildcards.
  Example:  BBS*.* or BBS
- The 'W' command prompt for WEB address was display the EMAIL prompt.  Fixed.
- Spacing of the field length guides '( )' was displaying incorrect for the
  EMAIL and WEB address prompts for NEWUSER logins and the 'W' command.
  Fixed.
- Fixed a bug in PCBoard to crash which exists since v15.3.  The following
  commands in PPL when used the following combination:
     USELMRS FALSE
     GETALTUSER 1
     ADDUSER "USERNAME", TRUE


04/22/97  11:22   PCBSM.EXE
===========================
- If a PCBoard PSA wasn't installed, you were still allowed to edit the
  information for the PSA.  Fixed.


04/22/97  16:48   PPLC.EXE
==========================
- Fixed a bug which caused PCBoard to crash with the following combination
  of PPL commands.
      USELMRS FALSE
      GETALTUSER 1
      ADDUSER "USERNAME", TRUE


04/22/97  12:04   UUIN.EXE
==========================
- Now supports 'multipart/alternative' MIME encoding.



04/18/97  10:10   PCBOARD.EXE
=============================
- Fixed the default 'M' for Gender to be empty until the user specifies
  either 'M' or 'F'.
- Chat Actions starting with the same first two letters or more common
  letters would always use the first one instead of waiting until a unique
  key was identified.
- After using a chat action, you had to press ENTER before using another one.
  Fixed.
- Fixed some small problems with the chat color support.
- Cleaned up some miscellaneous code to help reduces memory requirements a
  little.


04/18/97  11:10   PCBSM.EXE
===========================
- Fixed the default 'M' for Gender to be empty until the user specifies
  either 'M' or 'F'.




04/15/97  10:00
===============
- This is the first beta release of PCBoard v15.4.

